[I] Image processing system

[T] GraphicsMagick is the swiss army knife of image processing. It provides a
[T] robust and efficient collection of tools and libraries which support
[T] reading, writing, and manipulating an image in over 92 major formats.

[U] http://www.graphicsmagick.org/

[A] Graphicsmagick Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base
[F] CROSS

[E] opt ghostscript
[E] opt mbedtls
[E] opt jasper
[E] opt jbigkit
[E] opt lcms2
[E] opt libheif
[E] opt libjpeg
[E] opt libjxl highway
[E] opt libpng
[E] opt libtiff
[E] opt libwebp
[E] opt libzip

[L] MIT
[V] 1.3.49

[D] c175270b6cc3c84e07e3be59df667ad53525cb843c70e9819f90c7db GraphicsMagick-1.3.49.tar.xz https://downloads.sourceforge.net/graphicsmagick/graphicsmagick/1.3.49/

[ "$SDECFG_STATIC" = 1 ] || var_append confopt ' ' --enable-shared

pkginstalled libheif || var_append confopt ' ' --without-heif
pkginstalled libwebp || var_append confopt ' ' --without-webp
